### Advertising Active Measurement Groups in IGPs
- **Presentation**: [03-IGP Measurement Groups](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lsr-igp-measurement-groups-01)
- **Presenter**: Acee Lindem

Acee Lindem presented updates on advertising active measurement groups in IGPs:
- Extended scope beyond IS-IS to include OSPF and BGP-LS encodings.
- Reduced flooding overhead by advertising only a 16-bit Active Measurement Group ID and endpoint address in the IGP, while protocol types (e.g., STAMP, TWAMP) and parameters are configured locally per Group ID.
- In IS-IS, advertisements default to leaking between Level 1 and Level 2. In OSPFv2/OSPFv3, an AS-wide Router Information LSA is used.
- **Discussion**:
  - Tony Przygienda suggested handling IS-IS overload nodes similarly to unreachable nodes.
  - Shraddha Hegde and Rakesh Gandhi clarified that this mechanism automates discovery of active measurement reflectors across a network to automatically bring up measurement sessions.
  - Reshad Rahman highlighted that this auto-discovery eliminates heavy per-device manual configuration when onboarding new routers into full meshes.
  - Christian Hopps noted that adding configuration features to IGPs requires strong protocol-level justification, such as interaction with Traffic Engineering (TE) path selection.

