### Deprecating IPsec AH in OSPFv3
- **Presentation**: [04-OSPFv3 Deprecate IPsec AH](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lsr-ospfv3-deprecate-ipsec-ah-04)
- **Presenter**: Acee Lindem

Acee Lindem presented a proposal to deprecate RFC 4552 (IPsec Authentication Header (AH) usage for OSPFv3):
- Recommends using IPsec ESP with null encryption or OSPFv3 authentication trailers instead of AH, as AH provides no distinct advantage for OSPFv3 link-local traffic.
- **Discussion**:
  - Christian Hopps inquired about operational deployments of AH. Acee noted Cisco IOS-XE supports both ESP and AH, but deprecating AH over time is acceptable.
  - Les Ginsberg asked why formal deprecation is necessary instead of issuing an Informational RFC. Acee Lindem and Christian Hopps explained that the IPsec Working Group requires routing protocols to formally deprecate AH usage before IPsec specifications can deprecate AH globally.
  - The authors requested Working Group adoption.

