### IS-IS Hello Capability TLV
- **Presentation**: [05-Hello Capability](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lsr-05-hello-capability-00)
- **Presenter**: Les Ginsberg

Les Ginsberg presented a draft defining an interface-level Hello Capability TLV in IS-IS:
- Modeled after the IS-IS Router Capability TLV, it allows nodes to advertise optional per-interface or per-neighbor capabilities using a variable-length bitmask and sub-TLVs inside IS-IS Hellos (IIHs).
- Provides per-level support where applicable.
- **Discussion**:
  - Acee Lindem spoke in support of working group adoption.
  - Martin supported the proposal from an operator perspective, confirming that different levels often run under different operational parameters.
  - The authors requested Working Group adoption.

