### Fast Flooding Retransmission Indication
- **Presentation**: [07-Fast Flood RTX Indication](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lsr-fast-flood-rtx-indication-00)
- **Presenter**: Tony Przygienda

Tony Przygienda presented additions to IS-IS Fast Flooding (RFC 9081):
- Proposes explicit retransmission (RTX) indication to neighbors, allowing them to dynamically lower their advertised receive window (`rwin`) when loss/retransmission occurs.
- Uses short bursts of IIHs when shrinking `rwin` and applies hysteresis when reopening windows.
- Redefines `rwin` credit units per LSP fragment slot rather than raw bytes and couples Local Periodic Purge/Ack (LPP) directly to `rwin`.
- Includes a fallback mechanism to standard LSP transmit intervals if fast flooding collapses.
- **Discussion**:
  - Acee Lindem asked about implementation complexity compared to standard RFC 9081 fast flooding.
  - Tony Przygienda explained that without explicit RTX feedback, fast flooding window management collapses under high scale (e.g., hundreds of active peers competing for CPU/IO).

