### IS-IS Originating Generation Identifier (OGID)
- **Presentation**: [09-ISIS_OGID](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lsr-09-isis-ogid-01)
- **Presenter**: Shraddha Hegde

Shraddha Hegde presented a proposal to address transient route flaps caused by LSP fragment repacking:
- When new features (e.g., SRv6 SIDs) expand existing TLVs, descriptors can be pushed into adjacent fragments. Out-of-order reception of fragments by neighbors causes transient route flaps and traffic loss.
- Introduces the OGID TLV, carrying a transaction-based OGID counter, Last Resolvable GID (LRGID), and fragment count to correlate multi-fragment updates.
- Defines a "Soft Overload" bit for full repacking events to instruct receivers to hold SPF processing until repacking completes.
- **Discussion**:
  - Les Ginsberg and Acee Lindem voiced concern regarding implementation complexity (requiring nodes to track multiple database state copies) and questioned whether real-world gains justify the added state overhead compared to fast flooding and SPF hold-down timers.
  - Shraddha Hegde and Tony Przygienda countered that fragment repacking is causing real production network flaps in dense feature environments, justifying an optional signaling mechanism.

