### Detection of Router-ID Conflicts in IGPs
- **Presentation**: [11-Detection of Router-ID Conflicts in IGPs](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lsr-11-detection-of-router-id-conflicts-in-igps-00)
- **Presenter**: Liyan Gong

Liyan Gong presented a proposal to detect non-adjacent router-ID conflicts in IGPs:
- Monitors update frequency of self-originated LSAs/LSPs and compares payload inconsistency ratios (e.g., >83% mismatch in advertised interfaces/neighbors) on intermediate nodes to detect duplicate Router-IDs and emit YANG notifications to operators.
- **Discussion**:
  - Les Ginsberg and Acee Lindem noted that duplicate Router-ID detection and resolution mechanisms are already specified in existing RFCs (e.g., RFC 7503 for OSPFv3 auto-configuration using fingerprint TLVs).
  - Acee Lindem noted that standardizing YANG notifications for conflict detection could still be evaluated by the WG.

